# Repo hygiene deny-list — strings that must never appear in a public repo.
#
# This repo is public and AGPL-3.0. Naming the machines, networks, premises or
# people the software actually runs on discloses where the authors live and
# work, and git history is permanent: a leak is not undone by a later commit.
# #147 scrubbed two real premises out of the spec, an ADR and eleven test
# files; #211 scrubbed a real host name and a real home directory that the same
# reasoning had already condemned. This file exists so the third one fails a
# PR instead of being found by accident during unrelated work.
#
# WHAT BELONGS HERE
#   - Real host names, tailnet/LAN names and machine names.
#   - Real premises, estate, street or building names.
#   - Real people's names, usernames and home directories.
#   - Real deployment paths that identify a specific machine's disk layout.
#   - Real personal email addresses, and real routable addresses/subnets.
#
# WHAT DOES NOT
#   - Secrets. Credentials are a different class with a different response
#     (rotate, don't just delete); the provider-fixture credential scanner
#     (`make scan-fixtures`) owns those.
#   - Anything reserved for documentation and therefore SAFE to write down:
#     example.com/.org/.invalid, 192.0.2.0/24, 198.51.100.0/24, 203.0.113.0/24,
#     localhost, 127.0.0.1.
#
# FORMAT
#   One POSIX extended regular expression per line. Blank lines and lines
#   starting with `#` are ignored. Matching is case-insensitive, so write the
#   plain form. Adding a pattern is cheap; prefer a slightly broad one — a
#   false positive costs a placeholder rename, a false negative costs a
#   permanent public disclosure.
#
#   scripts/hygiene.sh and this file are excluded from the scan, because the
#   patterns are themselves literal matches for what they forbid.

# --- host and machine names (#211) ---
hyperion

# --- premises and site names (#147) ---
bartley
skyparc

# --- personal paths: a home directory names its owner (#211) ---
# Placeholder library paths in tests and docs use /srv/media instead.
/home/[a-z0-9]
/users/[a-z0-9]

# --- personal usernames ---
jaryl
